nd. Run 'bivvy init' first.\\\");\\n        return Ok(CommandResult::failure(2));\\n    }\\n    Err(BivvyError::ConfigParseError { path, message }) => {  // ONLY LintCommand does this\\n        ui.error(&format!(\\\"Parse error in {}: {}\\\", path.display(), message));\\n        return Ok(CommandResult::failure(1));\\n    }\\n    Err(e) => return Err(e),  // All other errors propagate up\\n};\\n```\\n\\n**Key Observations:**\\n- ConfigNotFound is handled gracefully with user-friendly message (exit code 2)\\n- ConfigParseError is ONLY explicitly handled in LintCommand\\n- Other commands let parse errors propagate as Err(e) to main.rs\\n- No explicit handling for ConfigValidationError in commands\\n- Main.rs catches any Err and shows generic error message + exit(1)\\n\\n### 7. **NO FALLBACK TO DEFAULT CONFIG**\\n\\n**Critical Finding:** There is NO fallback to default config. If `.bivvy/config.yml` doesn't exist:\\n- `ConfigPaths::has_project_config()` returns false\\n- `load_merged_config()` returns `BivvyError::ConfigNotFound`\\n- Commands all require an explicit config file\\n- User must run `bivvy init` to create one\\n\\n### 8. **Environment Variable Handling**\\n\\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/_q/qzh8_t6s15388qqf3p6n3d200000gp/T/bench-7okzbcvu/src/config/environment.rs`\\n\\n**Functions:**\\n- `load_env_file(path)` - Loads dotenv files, returns error if missing\\n- `load_env_file_optional(path)` - Returns empty map if missing (fallback)\\n- `load_system_env()` - Loads from system environment\\n- `merge_env(base, overlay)` - Merges environment variables\\n- Built-in SECRET_PATTERNS for masking sensitive values\\n\\n### 9. **Existing Warning/Error Infrastructure**\\n\\n**Config Module:**\\n- Tracing (via tracing crate) for debug logging\\n- ValidationError struct with categorized errors\\n- Comprehensive error types with context (paths, step names, etc.)\\n\\n**Lint Module** (`/src/lint/`):\\n- Rule-based diagnostics system\\n- Multiple formatters: Human, J