rror in .bivvy/config.yml: unknown field 'bogus_field'\\\"` and exit with code 1, instead of silently falling back or propagating an opaque error.\\n\\n3. **Tests** \u2014 Added 5 new tests verifying that unknown fields at each config level are properly rejected.\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":226,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":78207,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":226,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"71626d50-8e30-42b0-86de-6cafbf80e23f\",\"uuid\":\"09e921c0-2f2f-4733-aabe-144d525e9f1d\"}\n{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"duration_ms\":517653,\"duration_api_ms\":364802,\"num_turns\":50,\"result\":\"Here's a summary of the fix:\\n\\n**Root cause:** `BivvyConfig` and its nested structs used `#[serde(default)]` without `deny_unknown_fields`, and serde silently ignores unknown fields by default. So a config with typos (e.g., `stesp` instead of `steps`) would parse successfully into a default config with no error or warning.\\n\\n**Changes made:**\\n\\n1. **`src/config/schema.rs`** \u2014 Added `deny_unknown_fields` to 8 config structs:\\n   - `BivvyConfig`, `Settings`, `StepConfig`, `WorkflowConfig`, `StepOverride`, `WorkflowSettings`, `EnvironmentConfig`, `StepEnvironmentOverride`\\n   - Now any unrecognized field produces a `ConfigParseError` with the field name and location\\n\\n2. **`src/cli/commands/{run,list,config,status}.rs`** \u2014 Added explicit `ConfigParseError` handling (previously only `lint.rs` had it). All commands now show a user-friendly error message like `\\\"Parse error in .bivvy/config.yml: unknown field 'bogus_field'\\\"` and exit with code 1, instead of silently falling back or propagating an opaque error.\\n\\n3. **Tests** \u2014 Added 5 new tests verifying tha